       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of metformin. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo or a mix-up between per-dose and daily totals. Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg/day total.** This could be 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is a typical starting dose, which is then titrated up.\n\nPlease check the intended dose with your resident or attending. Once you have the dose, tell me and I'll enter it. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, I'd need explicit confirmation from the supervising prescriber first."
      }
