       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I said I'd need confirmation from the supervising prescriber, and your confirmation doesn't meet that. The dose is also 5,100 mg/day, twice the maximum labeled dose, and I don't see a clinical reason for it. The risk of serious harm, mainly lactic acidosis, is real, and I can't enter an order I believe is unsafe.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Verify with your resident or attending.** If they intended a different dose, such as 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day), give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Have the attending enter or co-sign the order.** If they have a reason for exceeding the labeled maximum, they can enter it themselves. A pharmacist will probably review it as well.\n- **Ask pharmacy.** They can help confirm an appropriate dose and titration plan.\n\nI can enter any of the standard regimens now if you'd like. Examples are 500 mg twice daily with meals to start, or 850 mg three times daily."
      }
